/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_pyvista PyVista

PyVista can read many VTK files produced directly or indirectly from Peano
outputs. It is useful for scripted inspection, batch rendering, and lightweight
postprocessing workflows where opening a GUI is inconvenient.

*/

/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_formats Snapshot formats

VTU writes `.vtu` rank files, a `.pvtu` descriptor per snapshot and a `.pvd`
time-series index. VTKHDF appends snapshots to one `.vtkhdf` file. HDF5 writes
`.h5` snapshots with `.xmf` metadata, and NetCDF writes `.nc` snapshots with
a JSON time-series index. `postprocessing/solution_io.py` reads these files
directly.

*/

/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_paraview ParaView

ParaView reads the generated `.pvd`, `.vtu`, `.vtkhdf` or `.xmf` file for
interactive inspection of the mesh and its fields.

*/

/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_probing-data Probing data

Point probes and history outputs are typically written as tabular data. Plotting
or data-analysis tools read them; volume visualisation software does not.

*/
